@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 48 and the Income Tax (Credits for Residents of the
-- Area) Order, 5755-1995. Row IL-28.
--
-- s 48 is a power: the Minister of Finance, with the approval of the Knesset
-- Finance Committee, may order that ss 34, 36 and 37, all or some of them, apply
-- "with the necessary changes" also to residents of the Area who are not Israeli
-- citizens, "as if they were Israeli residents". The Order of 1 March 1995 (one
-- section) did so for all three, for all such residents. The Order names ss 34,
-- 36 and 37 and no other section: it does not name s 36A, nor any section of
-- Chapter Three beyond those three.
--
-- Source quotations below are generated from the deposited files by
-- tools/srcquote.py and checked line by line by tools/hebcheck.py.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 48 and the Order of 5755-1995`

§§ `Section 3A(a) — an Israeli citizen, the Area, a resident of the Area`

-- s 48 takes its three terms from s 3A: ”אזור“, ”תושב אזור“ and ”אזרח ישראלי“.
-- src:ITO:455 | ”אזרח ישראלי“ – כל אחד מאלה:
-- src:ITO:456 | (1) אזרח ישראלי כמשמעותו בחוק האזרחות, התשי״ב–1952;
-- src:ITO:457 | (2) תושב ישראל;
-- src:ITO:458 | (3) מי שזכאי לעלות לישראל לפי חוק השבות, התש״י–1950, והוא תושב אזור;
-- src:ITO:459 | (4) חבר בני־אדם שאזרח ישראלי כמשמעותו בפסקאות (1) עד (3) הוא בעל שליטה בו; לענין זה, ”בעל שליטה“ – כהגדרתו בסעיף 32(9);
-- src:ITO:460 | ”אזור“ – כל אחד מאלה: יהודה והשומרון וחבל עזה כולל השטחים הכלולים בתחום השיפוט הטריטוריאלי של הרשות הפלסטינית על פי ההסכם בדבר רצועת עזה ואזור יריחו שנחתם בקהיר בין ישראל לבין ארגון השחרור הפלסטיני, ביום כ״ג באייר התשנ״ד (4 במאי 1994);
-- src:ITO:461 | ”תושב אזור“ – כהגדרת ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“ בסעיף 1, אלא שבכל מקום שנאמר שם ”בישראל“ קרי ”באזור“;

@ref ITO s 3A(a), lines 455-458
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` t MEANS
        t's `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`
    OR  t's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
    OR  (t's `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return` AND t's `a resident of the Area`)

-- A body of persons is limb (4) of the definition and is not asked about here: ss 34, 36 and 37 speak of an
-- individual, so nothing is extended to a body.
@ref ITO s 48, line 1807; s 3A(a), lines 455-461
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the taxpayer is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` t MEANS
        t's `an individual`
    AND t's `a resident of the Area`
    AND NOT `the taxpayer is an Israeli citizen within section 3A(a)` t

§§ `Section 48 — the power`

-- src:ITO:1806 | סעיף 48 – זיכויים לתושבי האזור [תיקון: תשכ״ב־2, תשמ״ד־10, תשמ״ז, תשנ״ה־3]
-- src:ITO:1807 | שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע בצו כי הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37, כולן או מקצתן, יחולו, בשינויים המחוייבים, גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כולם או חלקם, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל; לענין זה, ”אזור“, ”תושב אזור“ ו”אזרח ישראלי“ – כהגדרתם בסעיף 3א.
-- src:ITO:1808 | [note: פורסם צו מס הכנסה (זיכויים לתושבי האזור), התשנ״ה–1995, לפיו הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37 יחולו גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל.]

§§ `The Order — what it applies`

-- src:ORD:10 | בתוקף סמכותי לפי סעיף 48 לפקודת מס הכנסה, ובאישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, אני מצווה לאמור:
-- src:ORD:15 | הוראות סעיפים 34, 36 ו־37 יחולו גם לגבי תושבי אזור שאינם אזרחים ישראליים, כאילו היו תושבי ישראל.
-- src:ORD:17 | ⟦ח:חתימות|כ״ט באדר א׳ התשנ״ה (1 במרס 1995)⟧

-- The Order has one section, ”זיכויים לתושבי אזור“, and no commencement clause, no cut-off for the tax year and no
-- condition on the resident of the Area beyond ”שאינם אזרחים ישראליים“. It was signed on 1 March 1995
-- (ORD line 17), part-way through the 1995 tax year.

@ref ORD s 1, line 15
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Order reaches the taxpayer` t MEANS
    `the taxpayer is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` t

@ref ORD s 1, line 15; ITO s 48, line 1807
GIVEN p IS A `A provision of Chapter Three`
GIVETH A `What an instrument does to a provision`
`what the Order does to` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `section 34` THEN `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
    WHEN `section 36` THEN `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
    WHEN `section 37` THEN `applies the provision as if the taxpayer were an Israeli resident`
    OTHERWISE `leaves the provision as the provision itself reads`

§§ `The tax years the Order and the deposited text of s 3A govern`

@ref ITO s 48, line 1806 (last amendment תשנ״ה־3); ORD line 17
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding holds no order under section 48 for a tax year before 1995` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding holds no order under section 48 for a tax year before 1995"

@ref ITO s 3A, line 453 (last amendment תשע״ו־22, Hebrew year 5776, which ended 2 October 2016); ORD line 17
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995"

-- The Order carries no commencement clause. s 48 was last amended in תשנ״ה־3 and s 3A, whose three terms the Order
-- takes through s 48, in תשע״ו־22. As row IL-01 does (its fork F12, the lead's choice), the deposited text of a
-- section governs a tax year that begins after the Hebrew year of its last listed amendment has ended: 2017 for s 3A.
-- A year before 1995 precedes the Order; whether an earlier order under s 48 existed is not in the sources.
@ref ITO s 3A line 453; s 48 line 1806; ORD line 17
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Order and section 3A are held for the tax year of` t MEANS
    BRANCH IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 1995 THEN `this encoding holds no order under section 48 for a tax year before 1995`
           IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 2017 THEN `this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref ITO s 37, line 1599 (last amendment תשפ״ב, Hebrew year 5782, which ended 25 September 2022)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023` MEANS
    REFUSE "this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023"

§§ `Reading the case under the Order`

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; fork F2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point"

@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; fork F1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point"

@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; fork F4
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets"

@ref this row; input discipline
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the months of residence in the Area must be a whole number from 1 to 11` MEANS
    REFUSE "the months of residence in the Area must be a whole number from 1 to 11"

-- Fork F4, for the Order. Where the residence entered held for the whole tax year, every reading gives the
-- points for the year. For a resident of the Area for m months only: one status gives the points for the year;
-- apportioned gives 1/12 of a year's points for each month, as s 41(1) apportions ss 34 and 36; declined (the
-- default) where the two differ.
@ref ITO ss 34 and 36, lines 1570 and 1594; s 41(1), line 1691; fork F4
GIVEN t                                    IS A Taxpayer
      r                                    IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
      `the points for a year`              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points adjusted for part of a tax year in the Area, for` t `, under` r `, from` `the points for a year` MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year`
    WHEN `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year` THEN `the points for a year`
    WHEN `a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year` m THEN
        IF   m LESS THAN 1
          OR m AT LEAST 12
        THEN `the months of residence in the Area must be a whole number from 1 to 11`
        ELSE CONSIDER r's `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year`
             WHEN `one residence status for the whole tax year` THEN `the points for a year`
             WHEN `apportioned by the months of residence, as section 41 apportions`
                 THEN `the points for a year` TIMES m DIVIDED BY 12
             WHEN `declined for residence in part of a tax year`
                 THEN IF `the points for a year` EQUALS 0
                      THEN 0
                      ELSE `the Order does not say what a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year gets`

§§ `Section 34 under the Order`
-- src:ITO:1569 | סעיף 34 – זיכוי לתושב ישראל [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשכ״ח־2, תשל״א, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2]
-- src:ITO:1570 | בחישוב המס של יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס יובאו בחשבון שתי נקודות זיכוי.

-- "as if they were Israeli residents": the residence limb of s 34 is met, and the two points follow.
@ref ITO s 34, line 1570; ORD s 1, line 15
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 34 under the Order for` t `, under` r MEANS
    IF NOT t's `an individual`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the points adjusted for part of a tax year in the Area, for` t `, under` r `, from` 2

§§ `Section 36 under the Order`
-- src:ITO:1593 | סעיף 36 – זיכוי בעד נסיעה למקום ההשתכרות [תיקון: תשכ״ג, תשכ״ה, תש״ל, תשל״א, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשל״ז־4]
-- src:ITO:1594 | בחישוב המס של יחיד תושב ישראל תובא בחשבון 1 ⁄ 4 נקודת זיכוי כזיכוי נסיעה.

@ref ITO s 36, line 1594; ORD s 1, line 15; forks F2 and F4
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 36 under the Order for` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT t's `an individual` THEN 0
           IF t's `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year`
               THEN `the points adjusted for part of a tax year in the Area, for` t `, under` r `, from` (1/4)
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER r's `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion`
               WHEN `section 36 for every individual`
                   THEN `the points adjusted for part of a tax year in the Area, for` t `, under` r `, from` (1/4)
               WHEN `section 36 only for an individual with income from personal exertion` THEN 0
               WHEN `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`
                   THEN `section 36 does not say whether an individual without income from personal exertion gets its quarter point`

§§ `Section 36A — the Order does not name it`
-- src:ITO:1596 | סעיף 36א – זיכוי לאשה [תיקון: תשכ״ח־2, תשכ״ח־3, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשנ״ו]
-- src:ITO:1597 | בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1 ⁄ 2 נקודת זיכוי.

-- The Order names ss 34, 36 and 37. s 36A has no residence limb, so whether a woman who is a resident of the Area
-- and not an Israeli citizen gets its half point does not turn on the Order but on fork F1. Reading A: it has no
-- residence condition, she gets 1/2. Reading B: only an Israeli resident gets it; a resident of the Area who is not an
-- Israeli citizen is by s 3A(a)(2) never an Israeli resident, and the Order does not extend s 36A, so she gets 0.
@ref ITO s 36A, line 1597; ORD s 1, line 15; fork F1
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 36A, for a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen, for` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (t's `an individual` AND t's `a woman`) THEN 0
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER r's `fork F1, section 36A and residence`
               WHEN `section 36A has no residence condition` THEN 1/2
               WHEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident` THEN 0
               WHEN `declined where residence decides section 36A`
                   THEN `section 36A does not say whether a woman who is not an Israeli resident gets its half point`

§§ `Section 37 under the Order`
-- src:ITO:1599 | סעיף 37 – זיכוי בעד בן־ זוג [תיקון: תשכ״ה, תשל״ג, תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשנ״ב־6, תשס״ה־6, תשס״ו, תשפ״ב]
-- src:ITO:1600 | בחישוב המס של יחיד מוטב תושב ישראל, שהוכיח להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה כי בשנת המס שכלכלת בן זוגו היתה עליו, תובא בחשבון נקודת זיכוי אחת; לענין סעיף זה, ”יחיד מוטב“ – יחיד שהוא או שבן זוגו הגיע לגיל פרישה, או שהוא או שבן זוגו, עיוור או נכה כמשמעותם בסעיף 9(5)(א) או (א1).

@ref ITO s 37, line 1600; ORD s 1, line 15
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points under section 37 under the Order for` t MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT t's `an individual` THEN 0
           IF t's `the tax year` LESS THAN 2023 THEN `this encoding holds section 37 as it stood only from the tax year 2023`
           IF     t's `a favoured individual within section 37`
              AND t's `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`
              AND t's `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`
               THEN 1
           OTHERWISE 0

§§ `All four, for a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`

-- Asked of a person the Order does not reach, the Order's points are a question without an answer: the ordinary
-- sections (rows IL-01, IL-02, IL-08) govern that person, and a 0 here would read as their answer.
@ref ORD s 1, line 15
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Order does not reach the taxpayer, so its points are not asked` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Order does not reach the taxpayer, so its points are not asked"

@ref ITO s 48, line 1807; ORD s 1, line 15
GIVEN t IS A Taxpayer
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
GIVETH A `Credit points`
`the credit points the Order gives to` t `, under` r MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the taxpayer is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` t
               THEN `the Order does not reach the taxpayer, so its points are not asked`
           IF NOT `the Order and section 3A are held for the tax year of` t
               THEN `this encoding holds neither section 3A as it stood before 2017 nor the Order's start within 1995`
           OTHERWISE `Credit points` WITH
               `the points under section 34`  IS `the points under section 34 under the Order for` t `, under` r
               `the points under section 36`  IS `the points under section 36 under the Order for` t `, under` r
               `the points under section 36A` IS `the points under section 36A, for a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen, for` t `, under` r
               `the points under section 37`  IS `the points under section 37 under the Order for` t
